.TH start-mpd 1 "9 October 2025" "HiFiBerry" "HiFiBerry Audio Tools"
.SH NAME
start-mpd \- Start Music Player Daemon with user validation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B start-mpd
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B start-mpd
script is the startup wrapper for the Music Player Daemon (MPD) in HiFiBerry OS.
It performs user validation before starting MPD to ensure proper authorization.

The script first validates that the current user is authorized to run MPD by checking:
.IP \(bu 2
If running as root, start is allowed unconditionally
.IP \(bu 2
If running as a non-root user, the username must match the authorized user specified in /etc/hifiberry.user

If authorization fails, the script exits with code 0 to prevent systemd restart attempts.

After successful authorization, the script:
.IP \(bu 2
Calls configure-mpd to ensure proper MPD configuration
.IP \(bu 2
Starts MPD with the user-specific configuration file

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hifiberry.user
Contains the username authorized to run HiFiBerry services
.TP
.I ~/.etc/mpd.conf
User-specific MPD configuration file

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or authorization failure (to prevent systemd restart)
.TP
.B 1
Configuration or startup error

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR configure-mpd (1),
.BR mpd (1),
.BR mpd.conf (5)

.SH AUTHOR
HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>